PATCH 634: retain the reached resource registrar BX output and the caller EBX width.

Original 153c saves incoming BX around26fc (1557 POP BX), then 1594..159a uses
MOV AL,[SI]; MOV BL,[SI+1]; MUL BL; MOV BX,AX. Each descriptor product replaces
only BX; the last reached product returns at15be. A zero-length chain preserves
incoming BX, including E816 in the controlled empty startup case. The observed
40-record MSPRITE0 return is018f from dimensions1315, not a fixed resource ID.
Publish one WORD output owner, retaining the void indirect-call signature.
Original CB04 MOV BX,E816 leaves the upper EBX word unchanged; CB13..CB16 calls
e2fc with that complete DWORD. Consume the registrar result after it returns.
The full incoming EBX argument now travels through app_entry,0007 and00d0;
remove each uninitialized high-word constructor. Main passes its existing zero
argument; original app entry at cycle629918 actually has full EBX zero. Original
controlled89ab high word survives the complete registrar and returns89ab018f.

Sources: re_out/fist_dat_image.bin153c..15c1/CB04..CB18 and source-proven
resource_bx_case.json; complete original register/segment/flags/memory pairs in
scratch/sequence-capture/engine-resource-registers and resource-return-branches.
The original overflow15bf POP DS/STC/RET consumes a savedDS word as its return
IP; the existing C overflow return does not model that guest stack. This step
claims only the normal and empty BX/caller data contract. Loader CF, abnormal
stack return, CPU/IRQ timing, devices and full frame/mixed PCM remain open.
